V2.50 - 2026-11-06
	Stream-exit chord (Options + L3) now requires a 1-second hold to prevent accidental quits
	Native Options button mapping: physical Options sends Host Options (Start)
	Host PS / Guide button mapped to clean L1 + R1 + Options chord with pulse filter
	Touchpad click mapped directly to Host Touchpad / View / Select button
	Centered Settings overlay into a TV overscan-safe modal dialog
	Support hostname/DDNS manual host entry with smart port parsing
	Fix black screen on stream startup with hosts lacking on-demand IDR
	Fix manual host add duplicate check to consider port as well as IP/hostname
	Dedicated storage directory (/data/moonlight-mp/) with automatic legacy DX import
	High-fidelity Size 2 DualShock 4 active controller indicator icons in header
	Updated Moonlight MP branding for boot and splash screens
	Rendered 1080p documentation and menu artwork

V2.20 - 2026-11-05
	DualShock 4 dual-motor force feedback / rumble support (scePadSetVibration)
	Dynamic in-game RGB light bar color control (scePadSetLightBar)
	Advertised rumble and RGB LED capabilities in arrival events
	Independent per-controller rumble and LED routing
	Automatic vibration cutoff and LED reset on disconnect and stream exit

V2.10 - 2026-11-05
	Rebranded to Moonlight MP (multi-controller / multiplayer support)
	Added multi-controller support (simultaneous 2+ DualShock 4 controllers)
	Multi-user session discovery via sceUserServiceGetLoginUserIdList
	Per-controller light bar coloring (P1: Blue, P2: Red, P3: Green, P4: Magenta)
	Independent streaming controller routing with LiSendMultiControllerEvent
	Restricted mouse emulation touchpad to Controller 1
	Stream-exit chord (Options + L3) supported across any active controller
	Added reproducible Docker build container

V2.00 - 2026-09-12
	Full PS4 Pro Support
	HEVC and 4K streams implemented
	Shader uppdates for decoded HEVC conversion
	Added codec selection
	Added in-use codec to stream statistics overlay
	Added bitrate recommendation (Moonlight convention)
	Added resolution/framerate/bitrate dependet codec type selection
	Removed SPSfixup/h264bitstresm library: not needed, potentially detrimental
	Bug fixes in videodecoder configuration
	Fixed AudioOut intermittent audio failure on launch

V1.20 - 2026-09-09 (unreleased)
	Initial PS4 Pro support
	Full 4K UI and stream support (h264 only for now)
	unified video path for stream and non-stream UI
	base/neo mode dependent video_out configuration

V1.12 - 2026-09-08 (limited release)
	Added Bit Rate setting 10,25,50,75 Mbps
	Reversed CHANGELOG order

V1.11 - 2026-09-08
	Fixed an empty host list bug which resulted in button presses not working

V1.10 - 2026-09-07
	Change from multi-threaded CPU to GPU accelerated NV12->RGBA conversion 
	Color conversion to BT.709, more accurate for HD h264 streams
	Change stream overlays from CPU blit into frame buffer to GPU alpha blend
	Updated stream statistics to show total frame time.

v1.01 - 2026-09-05
	Fixed decoder starvation by increasing decode pipeline depth

v1.00 - 2026-09-05
	Initial Release